# Ancient Adamantoise's damage adds up across turns (CR 514.2: "Damage isn't removed from this creature during cleanup
# steps") until it is lethal (CR 704.5g), and "When this creature dies, exile it and create ten tapped Treasure tokens".
# Bot1 deals its own 20-toughness Adamantoise 17 with Fire Covenant (paying 17 life; its own spell, so ward does not
# trigger) on turn 3. The damage survives Bot1's cleanup. On turn 4 Bot2's Lightning Bolt at Bot1, who has 3 life, is
# dealt to the Adamantoise instead (a redirect of noncombat damage to a player): 20 damage, and it dies with Bot1 still at
# 3. Its trigger exiles the card from the graveyard and makes ten Treasures, all tapped, under Bot1's control.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Black Lotus
Show and Tell
Ancient Adamantoise
Forest
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Fire Covenant
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Show and Tell.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Ancient Adamantoise)
Bot2.Choose()
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Fire Covenant.Cast(X: 17)
Bot1.Divide(Ancient Adamantoise: 17)
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Life = 3
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ancient Adamantoise.Damage = 17
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ancient Adamantoise.Damage = 17
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 3
Exile = Ancient Adamantoise
Bot1.Graveyard = Fire Covenant; Show and Tell; Black Lotus
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 14
Bot1.Battlefield.Treasure Token#1.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Treasure Token#10.Tapped = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Treasure Token#10.Token = true
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
